#. Names on the dialogue box's name plate.
msgid "NPC_GUARD"
msgstr "Security Guard"

#. The security guard, before you've beaten the Warden. Night shift, nervous,
#. stuck at his post near the start. The "loading bay" is the Warden's arena.
msgid "DLG_GUARD_BEFORE_1"
msgstr "Whoa, easy there. Didn't think anyone still came down here."

msgid "DLG_GUARD_BEFORE_2"
msgstr "Night shift's been quiet since the lights went out. Too quiet."

msgid "DLG_GUARD_BEFORE_3"
msgstr "Something's holed up in the old loading bay past the shutter. Big. Armoured. I'd turn back if I were you."

#. The guard, before the Warden, on every later visit.
msgid "DLG_GUARD_BEFORE_AGAIN"
msgstr "Still here? That thing in the loading bay isn't going anywhere. Neither am I."

#. The guard, after you've beaten the Warden: thanks, and a warning about the
#. Harrier, which nests high up past the climb.
msgid "DLG_GUARD_AFTER_WARDEN_1"
msgstr "You took that thing down? I... thank you. Really."

#. The guard hands you a Strong Pipe (a heavier weapon), right after thanking you.
msgid "DLG_GUARD_AFTER_WARDEN_GIFT"
msgstr "Here, take this. Found it on my rounds. Hits a lot harder than that rusty thing."

msgid "DLG_GUARD_AFTER_WARDEN_2"
msgstr "But listen. Up past the climb, something's nesting in the rafters. Feathers like knives."

msgid "DLG_GUARD_AFTER_WARDEN_3"
msgstr "It sees you long before you see it. Keep moving, and watch the sky."

#. The guard, after the Warden, on every later visit.
msgid "DLG_GUARD_AFTER_WARDEN_AGAIN"
msgstr "Thanks again. And mind the rafters."

#. The guard, after you've beaten the Harrier too.
msgid "DLG_GUARD_AFTER_HARRIER_1"
msgstr "Both of them? You're something else."

msgid "DLG_GUARD_AFTER_HARRIER_2"
msgstr "Maybe I'll finally get some quiet on this shift."

#. The guard, after the Harrier, on every later visit.
msgid "DLG_GUARD_AFTER_HARRIER_AGAIN"
msgstr "Quiet nights from here on. I hope."
